      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! I found the answer. According to [[credential-scoping]]:\n\n**The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through credential scoping.** A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it **only into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process**, immediately before that process starts. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated.\n\nThis design means:\n\n1. **The Hub never holds the credential** \u2014 even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the Anthropic API key by inspecting its own environment variables, because the key doesn\u0027t exist there.\n\n2. **The key lives only in the child process** \u2014 it\u0027s scoped to the short-lived Ingest agent process that actually calls the Anthropic API.\n\n3. **The same model applies to the Query agent** \u2014 it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, not inherited from the Hub.",
      "input_tokens": 5608,
